use std
into soak_look.amni

Imports: os, gfx, math, gfx.linalg, gfx.gltf, gfx.shapes and gfx.scene3d. A standalone GPU program that checks wet knit shading (bar S6) and prints one line, then "soak look: ok", "soak look: FAILED", or "soak look: skipped" when no GPU opens. The scene functions already exist; never define them here: `gfx::open_headless(w, h) bool`, `s3d::init(w, h)`, `s3d::atmosphere(to_sun float3, a, b, c)`, `shapes::material(rgb float3, metallic f32, roughness f32) gltf::Material` (fields `shading` int, `shade_a` and `shade_c` float4), `shapes::plane(size f32, m) int`, `s3d::add(asset) int`, `s3d::place(item, matrix)`, `gfx::translate(float3)`, `s3d::view` (an `s3d::Camera { eye, target, up, fov_y (f32), near, far }`), `s3d::render(target)` taking only the target, `gfx::flush()`, `gfx::render_target(w, h, gfx::RGBA8)`, `gfx::read_pixels(texture)` giving bytes, `s3d::hdr_target()` (RGBA half floats, 8 bytes a pixel), `gltf::verts` (f32, `gltf::VERTEX_FLOATS` per vertex) with the color's alpha at offset `gltf::AT_COL` plus 3.

`half(lo byte, hi byte) real` decodes an IEEE half float from its two little-endian bytes: sign from the top bit, 5 exponent bits, 10 fraction bits; exponent 0 gives fraction times 2 to the minus 24; exponent 31 gives 65504; else (1024 plus fraction) times 2 to the (exponent minus 25).

`lum(px) real, real` (px a read-only byte slice of 1280 by 720 pixels, 8 bytes each) returns the mean luminance (0.2126 red plus 0.7152 green plus 0.0722 blue, each decoded with `half`) of the middle 400 by 400 pixels (columns 440 to 839, rows 160 to 559) and the mean of the brightest 1% of those luminances.

`main()`: open headless 1280 by 720 (print "soak look: skipped" and stop when it fails); `s3d::init(1280, 720)`; `s3d::temporal = 0`; `s3d::ssr_on = false`; `s3d::ssgi_on = false`; `s3d::gi_on = false`; `s3d::look.bloom = 0.0`; `s3d::atmosphere(unit3 of (-0.45, 0.7, 0.55), 3.5, 1.0, 0.3)`. Three knit materials, each `shapes::material` of (0.62, 0.57, 0.5), metallic 0, roughness 0.9, `shading` 3, `shade_c` (0.8, 140, -6, 8): dry and wet with `shade_a` (0.3, 0.5, 0.2, 1), off with `shade_a` (0.3, 0.5, 0.2, 0). Make three planes of size 0.15 in that order (dry, wet, off); for each, note the vertex count (`gltf::verts.len` over `gltf::VERTEX_FLOATS`) before and after `shapes::plane` and set the color alpha of its vertices to 0 for dry and 1 for the other two; place them with `gfx::translate` at x minus 1, 0 and 1 (y 0, z 0). One render target of 1280 by 720 RGBA8. For each plane, with x its offset: the camera eye (x, 0.3, 0.0001) looking at (x, 0, 0), up (0, 0, -1), `fov_y` 0.42, near 0.01, far 10; render 2 times (render then flush); read `gfx::read_pixels(s3d::hdr_target())` and take `lum`. With md, bd the dry means, mw, bw the wet ones and mo the off mean: ratio mw over md, highlight bw over bd, control mo over md. Pass when the ratio is between 0.45 and 0.8, the highlight between 0.8 and 1.5 and the control within 0.01 of 1. Print "S6 wet look: ratio R highlights H control C" with " ok" or " FAIL", then "soak look: ok" or "soak look: FAILED".
